 is sort of a  different story  but what they're saying is they'll tweak  the algorithm so that if you're just  searching around for information on some  of these topics  you're not going to get conspiracy  videos placed  in front of you how much content will  this impact youtube says that this will  impact less than one percent of all  content on youtube and again this is not  about whether the content is or isn't  allowed that's not changing  um the reactions have been pretty  predictable some so-called free speech  absolutists are saying  it's censorship this is an attack on  constitutionally protected free speech  and they're saying all of the things  you would anticipate they would say  other people are saying well hold on a  second  youtube can decide what content it wants  to promote  and what content it doesn't want to  promote the recommendation algorithm  is merely how youtube expresses what it  wants to put a spotlight on  and what it doesn't nothing illegal is  happening here  is uh uh is this something that could  inadvertently hurt people who aren't  doing anything wrong  sure yeah i mean people spreading  misinformation  are going to be hurt by this and they're  going to be at a disadvantage  but people who are also doing great  stuff are going to probably end up  inadvertently caught up in this as well  here's the reality the recommendation  algorithm on youtube  has always favored some content over  others  it's changing all the time it's never  worked perfectly the david pakman show  youtube channel  has been hurt by algorithm changes  at different points in time we've had  content that didn't do as well  because of how the algorithm is  configured we've had content that was  pushed viral  on a whim that we didn't even understand  because of the algorithm  i think that if we are given the choice  between knowing more about how the  algorithm works  and knowing less i prefer to know more  at least they're being upfront about  this tweak what people 